  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "config-melcoe-pep.xml defines the predicates that are used in forming the XACML hierarchical resource identifier used in specifying policies for example for collection members in the form /collection:1/.* - which specifies \"all children of collection:1\".  The relationships are used in identifying what the children are.  For example \"isMemberOf\".",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Currently only child-parent relationships are allowed (and incorrectly identified as parent-child relationships).  It would be useful to also allow parent-child relationships for those situation where it is the RELS-EXT of the collection that identifies its members rather than the children using isMemberOf to specify the parent.  (The current relsext relationship ontology has both isMemberOf and hasMember).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Changes:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "1. Correct existing config files and code to identify current relationships as child-parent instead of parent-child",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2.  Add ability to specify parent-child relationships",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
